`theorem refute_e20263a9 : ¬ Candidate`, editing the file in place. Leave the other theorem untouched with its `sorry`.\n  - Preserve everything above the first `theorem` line unchanged. Helper lemmas must be top-level declarations placed after `Candidate`.\n  - Disallowed: `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide`, `namespace`, `section`, `variable`, `notation`, `macro`, `syntax`, `IO`, metaprogramming, and running `lake`.\n  - Allowed axioms: only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n  - Verification script: `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh <file.lean>`.\n  - Deliverable: Update `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and write `REPORT.md` documenting settled direction, key mathematical idea, and checker output.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Direction Settled**: The conjecture is **TRUE** (`prove_e20263a9`). Zero counterexamples exist across the complete Graph Atlas (all 995 connected graphs $n \\le 7$), all non-isomorphic trees up to $n = 16$, random graphs, paths, and cycles.\n- **Formally Verified Lean 4 Lemmas (compiled with exit code 0 & standard axioms)**:\n  - `minUpTo_le`\n  - `radius_le_eccentricity`\n  - `le_romanDominationNumber`: reduces `radius G + 1 ≤ romanDominationNumber G` to `∀ f, IsRomanDominatingFunction G f → radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`.\n  - `two_le_romanWeight`: for any Roman dominating $f$ on a nontrivial graph, $2 \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n  - `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: if no vertex has label 2, $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n  - `radius_add_one_le_card`: $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$ via strict `ballWithin` expansion.\n  - `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: if $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$, then $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n  - `ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all`: if $\\forall w, w = u \\lor G.Adj\\ u\\ w$, then $\\text{ballWithin } G\\ 1\\ u = \\text{univ}$.\n  - `radius_le_one_of_adj_all`: if $u$ is adjacent to all other vertices, $\\text{radius}(G